Subject: [PATCH 065/162] hjviewer: the gate's words after the first day
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

U01: one name per password. The PC's own password box says "원격 PC
비밀번호" (Remote PC password), says whose password it takes and that
it is not the access or the portal password, names its field "PC
비밀번호", and a wrong one is "PC 비밀번호가 맞지 않습니다". After A1
took the access password, that box shows once on top that the access
password is done; the toast stays for a port forward only. A1 says the
PC asks for its own password, and its title and field carry the key
icon, as P2 does. The login names its second field "연세포탈 비밀번호"
and its empty fields by their names. Settings and the login notice say
"영구 비밀번호" for this PC's own password; the password card's pencil
and the set-password dialog say "Set permanent password".

U02: "Remote desktop is offline" from a staff-only server says the PC
may be up but nobody logged in or entered the access password on it,
as a condition while the mode is unknown; after A1 it says the access
password was fine and that PC is the one missing. Only the shown text
changes, so the 30-second retry still sees the key. A desktop session
window now asks the server's mode too.

U03: while the server may be staff-only, the login notice no longer
offers a logout to turn password-less connections off, and its
permanent password hint says a logout locks the PC out. The empty
device list drops "1.6.0 or later". On a staff-only server the outage
banner says new logins and the access password stop too. G1 and G2
name the 12-hour limit and the restart and Windows sign-out ends. The
main window's close asks once per access password ticket whether to
end it: [끝내고 닫기] [계속 받기]; dismissing it keeps the window.

U06: a logged-in PC that hbbs refuses shows nothing for about a
minute, then "로그인했지만 서버가 이 PC를 받지 않고 있습니다" with the
account card's cause and button ([다시 추가], [다시 로그인]), or that it
is checked again. Its status line and tray drop "(로그인 필요)"; the
tray takes a non-empty hjv-pwless-state for a login.

U09: P1's title loses "아직" and its text says what the login is for;
its second button is the action "이용 비밀번호 넣기" while P2's dialog
keeps its name. "연결받다" becomes "연결을 받다" in P2's line, its end
toast and E4. E1 says what to do next.

U20: the status line says "서버에 연결하는 중…" and "서버에 연결할 수
없습니다. 네트워크 연결을 확인해 주세요." (ko.rs and en.rs). While
refused, the tray puts the state in place of "Ready" or "Service is
running" instead of adding a line that contradicts it.

U67: the remote restart's confirm says, by the server's mode, that a
PC nobody logged in on cannot be reached after the restart until
someone logs in or enters the access password there, and that HJViewer
that is not installed does not start again. A session that asked for
the restart adds that to its offline text. P2's dialog names the
restart and Windows sign-out ends, and a refusal that starts again
clears P2's end time, so a dead P2 line does not come back.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
